From b9f323756e483e673662f2211095c7f06387d388 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:51:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 05/26] ling: EXL3 routed experts in Ling's clamp order,
 min(silu(g), L) * clip(u, -L, L), on the shared grouped finish's twin

exl3_experts.cu's plan finish becomes a template: tf_exl3_plan_finish keeps the clamp on silu's input
(its sm_121 SASS unchanged, as every other function of the image), tf_exl3_plan_finish_after clamps
silu's output. exl3_grouped launches the twin for experts.Layer.after; the Ling loader sets it and the
SwiGLU limit, so the clamped layers 65-71 load on EXL3. ling-exl3-clamp checks a real EXL3 layer's
grouped gate-up against float64 on its own g and u (read through the same kernels as down projections),
with an unclamped control and GLM's order told apart.
